<title>GERMANY: Waigel-will take budget steps to hit deficit goal.</title>
<headline>Waigel-will take budget steps to hit deficit goal.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Thursday that Germany would meet the 3.0 percent Maastricht Treaty deficit criteria for entry to European economic and monetary union (EMU) in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;We will take measures in the budget to reach 3.0,&quot; Waigel told German television, referring to the Maastricht treaty target for the budget deficit to gross domestic product (GDP) ratio in 1997.</p>
<p>Waigel said earlier, however, than he was not prepared to engage in a discussion over decimal points in EMU criteria, stressing that credibility of convergence was more important.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
